        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d4707755-962d-53f4-8b98-f7cf0dc443e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lancaster, Lancashire, England, Peel, Isle of Man, Fleetwood\n- Organizations: Roman Catholic Diocese of Lancaster\n- Buildings: Lancaster Cathedral, Peel Cathedral, St Mary's Church\n- Concepts: Roman Catholic parish church, cathedral, Latin Rite\n\nFacts:\n- Peel Cathedral, also called the Cathedral Church of Saint German and rebranded as Cathedral Isle of Man, is located in Peel on the Isle of Man.\n- Peel Cathedral was built between 1879 and 1884.\n- Peel Cathedral is one of the parish churches in the parish of the West Coast, which includes the town of Peel.\n- Lancaster Cathedral, also known as The Cathedral Church of St Peter and Saint Peter's Cathedral, is on St Peter's Road in Lancaster, Lancashire, England.\n- Lancaster Cathedral was a Roman Catholic parish church until 1924, when it was elevated to cathedral status.\n- The Roman Catholic Diocese of Lancaster is a Latin Rite Roman Catholic diocese centred on Lancaster Cathedral in Lancaster, Lancashire, England.\n- St Mary's Church, Fleetwood is an active church in the Roman Catholic Diocese of Lancaster.",
